I launched the third seed for the "compressor frozen" arm. Nothing is decided yet, and nothing is needed from you.

## Done this wake
- **"Connector frozen" arm, seed 42: training finished.** It ran 1 epoch (27,936 rows) in 11.2 h at 33.8 GB peak GPU memory.
  - The check on which weights moved shows the freeze held: the connector (the small network between compressor and decoder) did not change, while the compressor and decoder adapters trained.
  - Held-out loss at the end is .434 (lower is better). The reference run is at .414 and the two earlier frozen arms at .435. These are only 64 rows with no paired test, so it is a health signal, not a result.
- **"Compressor frozen" arm, seed 44: launched.** The first two seeds gave a tie under the campaign rules (documents −2.9 / −3.9 points, MRQA text −2.3 / −3.1), and the rules call for a third seed in that case. I submitted six jobs in one chain, which is the per-wake limit:
  - the finetune, started 02:32 on an A100;
  - four evals (documents, photos, two text sets) that start when it finishes;
  - the weight-movement check.
- **Fixed what the read-only checker flagged.** The two-seed tie result now has a recorded verdict. The claim "compressor-frozen equals fully-frozen" is softened to what the confidence intervals actually show.

## Running now
| What | State | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| Connector frozen, seed 43 (training) | 77% of 1 epoch; held-out loss .461, under the kill line of .471 (one earlier reading was above it) | ends ~05:05 |
| Connector frozen, seed 42 (4 evals) | waiting in the preemptible queue | start ~07:30 |
| Pass/fail test for the connector-frozen arm | waits on all 8 of its evals | late morning 11-14 |
| Compressor frozen, seed 44 (training + 4 evals) | training | ~12:30–14:00 |

## Things to know
- My new seed-44 finetune bumped this campaign's own documents eval off the same node. That eval went back into the queue automatically, and nothing was lost.
- I can't confirm the eval settings (image size, chunk length) reached the four queued evals until they write their output files. The same launch method gave correct file names for seed 43. I added a +1 to the open tool complaint about this.
- Budget: about 107 of 192 GPU-hours used; about 19 more planned.

## Next
The next wake comes when seed 43 of the connector-frozen arm finishes and its weight check runs, at most 4 hours from now. It will:
- read that run's last two held-out losses against the kill line;
- read the first held-out loss of compressor-frozen seed 44;
- submit seed 44's pass/fail test and its quarter-run preview eval.

Still open from earlier: the split-freeze code in `pisco/model.py` and `test_freeze.py` is still not committed. One of your chats should commit it, because the running jobs use it straight from the working tree.
